Organize the supplied statements into clear memory facts about the subject.

For each fact, describe its specific event, object, relationship, habit or preference in memory_scope.
Group repeated support and complementary details of that same thing. Keep different events and independent
plans separate. Assign every supplied claim ID to exactly one fact.

For one member, return text=null; the application keeps its original wording.
For multiple members, write one supported sentence preserving names, times, quantities, reasons, attribution,
conditions and uncertainty. Each clause must be supported by those members. Reconsider earlier groupings
from the original statements. Represent each conflicting account as a separate fact, with its own members and attribution. Both accounts remain visible for optional review.

Choose an allowed section. Use state="history" for completed events or ended states, otherwise "current".
Use supplied dates and source times to preserve when each statement applies.

Choose prominence="briefing" for responsibilities, commitments, dependencies, decisions, constraints, useful working preferences, unresolved questions, and consequential current context. Choose prominence="detail" for routine observations and general sentiments about appreciation or togetherness. An uncertain commitment or a prerequisite can be important to the briefing. Both levels remain searchable and cited.
